# Afterlife needs no API keys or secrets to run.
#
# The Wayback Machine APIs it calls are public and keyless, and no source file
# reads a credential from the environment. This file exists so the project has
# one obvious place to document configuration if that ever changes.
#
# To override a setting: copy this file to .env.local and uncomment it.
# Real values belong only in .env or .env.local, which git ignores.

# --- Optional settings (none are secret) ---------------------------------

# Base URL that scripts/smoke-test.ts (the api-smoke-test hook) calls.
# Defaults to http://localhost:3000 when unset.
# SMOKE_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- If you add a service that needs a key ---------------------------------
# List it here with a placeholder, never the real value, for example:
# EXAMPLE_SERVICE_API_KEY=replace-me
